# Shell scripts must always check out with LF line endings. A CRLF shebang line
# (`#!/usr/bin/env bash` followed by `\r\n`) fails to execute on Linux/macOS -- the kernel looks up an
# interpreter literally named `bash\r` and reports "No such file or directory" or "bad interpreter".
# Windows dev boxes commonly run with core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise convert these to CRLF on
# checkout; this forces LF regardless of that per-user setting, for every clone.
*.sh text eol=lf
